# Regression: a `print` in tail/return position must NOT leak the printf
# byte-count into main's i32 exit slot. `print` lowers to a UNIT result
# (mirrors Rust gg's `Constant::Unit`), so this expr-body main exits 0, not 3
# (the byte length of "tail-print-ok\n"). See the self-host is_print arm in
# tests/fixtures/self_host_lowerer/lower_expr.gg.
void main(): print("tail-print-ok")
